 "content": "# Continual-ARC pattern note: color-keyed stacked motif\n\nObserved task 07b463a7. A repeated simple silhouette (here a 3x6 pixel motif) appears in one or more colors, alongside a color key. The key lists colors in order: if vertical, read top-to-bottom; if horizontal and repeated identically over several rows, read left-to-right. Output removes/ignores the key and stacks one copy of the motif per key color, in key order, retaining motif pixel geometry and using each key color. Existing copies are preserved in their matching slots; add/recolor the motif copies to complete the ordered sequence. In the solved test, key [2,3,1,8,7] produced five vertically stacked 3-row copies at rows 0-14, leaving bottom rows blank. Demo with key [4,1,6] produced motif copies in that order at rows 2-6, 7-11, 12-16 (preserving the centered motif's spacing/positioning from the example).\n"
